eed2015310047/4/prompt.md:393:   - ✓ 真两层：\\\"通过孔洞数量匹配颜色图例\\\"→\\\"用匹配到的颜色重绘对象\\\" — 两步都需要非平凡的归纳。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/eval/seed1172698180/5/codegen_prompts/5.retry1.codex.log:2553:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1172698180.arc-codegen-similar/5/codegen_prompts/2.md:11:<new_puzzle index=\\\"2\\\">\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/eval/seed1172698180/5/codegen_prompts/5.retry1.codex.log:2669:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1172698180.arc-codegen-similar/5/codegen_prompts/2.codex.log:25:<new_puzzle index=\\\"2\\\">\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/eval/seed1172698180/5/codegen_prompts/5.retry1.codex.log:2820:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1172698180.arc-codegen-similar/5/codegen_prompts/2.retry1.codex.log:25:<new_puzzle index=\\\"2\\\">\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/eval/seed859803968/_codegen_logs_rerun/2_2.log:25:<new_puzzle index=\\\"2\\\">\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/eval/seed412606280/4/codegen_prompts/2.md:11:<new_puzzle index=\\\"2\\\">\\n/home/好只在一条对称轴的一侧。\\\\n\\\\n- `Rule`：\\\\n  - 保持边缘标记像素不变。\\\\n  - 对每条对称轴，找到位于其一侧的所有碎片。\\\\n  - 将每个碎片沿该对称轴做镜像翻折，在对称位置绘制翻折后的副本（使用碎片原来的颜色）。\\\\n  - 原始碎片保留不变。\\\\n  - 如果翻折后的副本与原始碎片（同一碎片或不同碎片）发生像素重叠，重叠位置的像素变为 Yellow。\\\\n  - 翻折副本不覆盖边缘标记像素。\\\\n\\\\n- `Key insight`：\\\\n  - 解题者首先需要从边缘标记中推断出隐含的对称轴（第一层），再确定每个碎片归属于哪条轴并执行镜像操作（第二层），最后理解重叠区域的特殊着色规则（第三层）——对称轴的存在不直接可见，必须通过边缘标记的位置关系推断。\\\\n</new_puzzle>\\\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1030756833/13/prompt.md\\\\n你是一个 ARC-AGI 谜题设计专家。下面的 20 道参考题是难度和机制质量的标杆。仔细阅读每道题的**解题逻辑**（解题者从样例归纳规则的认知过程），而非表面场景。你的新题应在机制深度和隐蔽性上与参考题持平或者实现超越。\\\\n\\\\n每个参考题描述包含：\\\\n- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。\\\\n- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\\\\n- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\\\\n- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\\\\n\\\\n参考题目如下：\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"1\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"train\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"9f669b64\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"26-48\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nPush the central solid rectangle to the grid edge, splitting the perpendicular target rectangle around its path.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure\\\\n- The background is the dominant color.\\\\n- There are exactly three monochrome foreground objects arranged on one\\\\n  horizontal or vertical axis.\\\\n- The middle object on that axis is a solid rectangular moving object.\\\\n- One end object is a solid rectangle or bar whose long side is perpendicular\\\\n  to the movement axis; this is the target to split.\\\\n\\\\nRule\\\\n- Move the middle rectangle along the axis toward the target until it is\\\\n  flush with the grid edge in that direction.\\\\n- Clear the original middle rectangle and the original target.\\\\n- Split the target through the moving rectangle's two-cell-wide path and\\\\n  shift the two halves one cell outward perpendicular to the movement.\\\\n- Keep the other end object unchanged.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight\\\\n- The non-target end object acts as a pusher; the central rectangle travels\\\\n  away from it through the perpendicular target, opening a matching gap.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"2\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"train\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"bc93ec48\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"48-63\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nCopy each foreground object anchored in a true grid corner clockwise into the next corner.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure\\\\n- The dominant color is the background.\\\\n- Foreground objects are monochromatic 4-connected components.\\\\n- Relevant objects are exactly those whose bounding box touches two adjacent borders at one grid corner.\\\\n\\\\nRule\\\\n- Start from the input unchanged.\\\\n- For each corner object, copy its pixel mask and color to the next corner clockwise: top-left to top-right, top-right to bottom-right, bottom-right to bottom-left, and bottom-left to top-left.\\\\n- Preserve each object's orientation by aligning its bounding box to the destination corner; stamps may overwrite existing pixels at the destination, but source pixels are not cleared.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight\\\\n- Interior and side-only objects are distractors; only components actually anchored to a corner participate in the clockwise perimeter copy.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"3\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"train\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"5a719d11\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"44-59\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nWithin each horizontal pair of two-color panels, swap the motif masks and recolor each pasted mask with the source panel's base color.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure:\\\\n- A separator color forms full blank rows and at least one full blank column.\\\\n- The non-separator area is split into row bands, each containing exactly two same-shaped rectangular panels.\\\\n- Each panel has a dominant base color and one minority motif color.\\\\n\\\\nRule:\\\\n- For every row band, clear each panel to its own base color.\\\\n- Paste the right panel's motif mask into the left panel using the right base color.\\\\n- Paste the left panel's motif mask into the right panel using the left base color.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight:\\\\n- The motif colors themselves are distractors; only each motif's shape mask and the two panel base colors are exchanged.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"4\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"train\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"58c02a16\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"10-26\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nExpand the top-left seed mask into a recursive colored pattern and tile it across the full grid.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure\\\\n- The background is the dominant color.\\\\n- All foreground lies in a top-left rectangle whose last row and last column are a solid secondary color.\\\\n- Removing that secondary-color row and column leaves a seed region containing background plus one primary color.\\\\n\\\\nRule\\\\n- Use the primary-color pixels in the seed as a binary mask.\\\\n- Replace each primary seed cell with a copy of the seed mask in the primary color, and each background seed cell\\\\n  with a copy of the seed mask in the secondary color.\\\\n- Repeat and crop that expanded tile to the original grid shape.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight\\\\nThe solid L-shaped secondary-color border is a legend, not output content; it supplies the color used when the\\\\nseed's background cells are expanded.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"5\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"train\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"54dc2872\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"52-69\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nMove each marked L-shaped sprite onto the separate pixel matching its marker color.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure\\\\n- The background is the dominant color.\\\\n- Foreground has 4-connected multicolor sprites and isolated one-pixel controls.\\\\n- Each sprite has one repeated body color in an L shape plus one embedded marker\\\\n  pixel of a different color.\\\\n\\\\nRule\\\\n- If the embedded marker color also appears as a separate isolated control pixel,\\\\n  translate the whole sprite so the body L-bend lands on that control pixel.\\\\n- Clear each moved sprite from its old position, clear its consumed control pixel,\\\\n  then paste all translated sprites; sprites without a matching control stay put.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight\\\\n- The marker color pairs a sprite with its destination control, while the L-bend\\\\n  gives the orientation-independent anchor cell to place on that destination.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"6\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"train\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"3cd86f4f\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"6-18\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nShear the rectangular input down-left onto a black canvas.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure\\\\nA rectangular grid of colored pixels with no internal empty region to infer.\\\\n\\\\nRule\\\\nCreate a black output with the same height and width W + H - 1, then copy\\\\neach input row r unchanged starting at column H - 1 - r.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight\\\\nThe colors and row contents are preserved; only the row offsets change so\\\\nthe left edge forms a descending diagonal.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"7\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"train\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"9841fdad\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"15-39\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nExpand the colored runs from the left reference panel into the blank right panel.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure:\\\\n- A uniform rectangular frame surrounds the grid.\\\\n- One full-height divider of the frame color splits a left reference panel\\\\n  from a blank right panel.\\\\n- Both panels have one background margin column on each side of their active\\\\n  columns; the left active columns contain two-column endpoint slots, possibly\\\\n  connected by same-color horizontal runs.\\\\n\\\\nRule:\\\\n- Keep the original grid and paint only in the right panel's active columns.\\\\n- A source run exactly matching the left endpoint slot is copied to the left\\\\n  two columns of the right active span.\\\\n- A source run exactly matching the right endpoint slot is copied to the right\\\\n  two columns of the right active span.\\\\n- A source run connecting the endpoint slots is stretched across the entire\\\\n  right active span.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight:\\\\nThe left panel is a compressed legend for the right panel: endpoint markers\\\\nstay two pixels wide, while connectors between endpoints expand to fill the\\\\ndistance between them.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"8\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"train\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"880c1354\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"14-28\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nRecolor the separated outer regions by rotating their colors one step clockwise around the yellow-orange divider.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure:\\\\n- The grid contains a fixed yellow/orange divider structure.\\\\n- All other colors form separated 4-connected monochrome regions around that divider.\\\\n\\\\nRule:\\\\n- Leave the yellow and orange pixels unchanged.\\\\n- Sort the non-divider regions by their centroid angle around the divider centroid in screen-coordinate clockwise order.\\\\n- Each region keeps its cells and receives the color of the previous region in that cyclic order.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight:\\\\n- The objects do not move; only the color labels cycle through the spatial order of the regions around the divider.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"9\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"train\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"78e78cff\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"71-91\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nRecolor the row-wise passage indicated by wall pixels with the singleton marker color.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure:\\\\n- A dominant background contains one singleton marker pixel and one wall color.\\\\n- Wall pixels lie on several rows and form left/right limits around the marker column.\\\\n- Empty rows between the top and bottom wall rows are open horizontal passages.\\\\n\\\\nRule:\\\\n- On a wall row, paint background pixels between the nearest wall strictly\\\\n  left of the marker column and the nearest wall at or right of it; if only\\\\n  one side is present, paint from that wall to the opposite grid edge.\\\\n- On empty rows between the top and bottom wall rows, paint the whole row.\\\\n- On empty rows outside the wall-row band, reuse the nearest end wall-row interval.\\\\n- Preserve wall pixels and the original marker pixel.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight:\\\\n- The wall color defines scanline limits relative to the marker column; the\\\\n  marker color fills those implied horizontal spans rather than flood-filling\\\\n  through connected background.\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/eval/seed454434671/_codegen_logs/1_2.log:27:<new_puzzle index=\\\"2\\\">\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/eval/seed1699747228/1/prompt.md:392:   - ✓ 真两层：\\\"通过孔洞数量匹配颜色图例\\\"→\\\"用匹配到的颜色重绘对象\\\" — 两步都需要非平凡的归纳。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/eval/seed12780398/1/codegen_prompts/2.md:11:<new_puzzle 